GitHub</span>\n   280→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-03</span>\n   281→                    </div>\n   282→                </div>\n   283→\n   284→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   285→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/LocalKinAI/kin-code\" target=\"_blank\">Kin Code</a></div>\n   286→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Lightweight AI coding assistant for your terminal written in Go. Single 10MB binary with zero dependencies. Features MCP support and Soul files for custom AI personas.</div>\n   287→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   288→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   289→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   290→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   291→                    </div>\n   292→                </div>\n   293→\n   294→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   295→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/iabhisekbosepm/custom_agent\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Agents</a></div>\n   296→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Terminal-based AI coding assistant running entirely on your machine with 5 specialized agents and 35+ built-in tools. Like Claude Code but you own it.</div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   298→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   299→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   300→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   301→                    </div>\n   302→                </div>\n   303→\n   304→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   305→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/mitja-kurath/daniel\" target=\"_blank\">Daniel</a></div>\n   306→                    <div class=\"product-description\">The proactive AI software engineer that lives in your terminal. Navigates directories, executes commands, fixes bugs across multiple files, and manages development lifecycle autonomously.</div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   308→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   309→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   310→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   311→                    </div>\n   312→                </div>\n   313→\n   314→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   315→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/cry-nix/MultiCode\" target=\"_blank\">MultiCode</a></div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Terminal AI coding buddy that reads files, edits code, and runs commands. Free and open-source alternative to Claude Code working with any model via OpenRouter.</div>\n   317→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   318→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   319→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   320→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   321→                    </div>\n   322→                </div>\n   323→\n   324→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   325→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/prithvi-45/memforge\" target=\"_blank\">memforge</a></div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Persistent memory MCP server for AI coding agents. Install once, your agents never forget. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Aider.</div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   328→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">code agent</span>\n   329→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   330→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                </div>\n   333→\n   334→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   335→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/MauricioPerera/oxshell\" target=\"_blank\">OxShell</a></div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"product-description\">AI coding assistant for the terminal powered by Cloudflare Workers AI, built in Rust. Can read files, write code, run commands, search codebases, and execute declarative workflows.</div>\n   337→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   338→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   339→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   340→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-01</span>\n   341→                    </div>\n   342→                </div>\n   343→\n   344→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   345→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/albertgd/free-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Free Claude Code</a></div>\n   346→                    <div class=\"product-description\">AI coding assistant for the terminal that works exactly like Claude Code but connects to Groq (free tier), OpenAI, or Google Gemini instead of Anthropic's API.</div>\n   347→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   348→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   349→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   350→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-01</span>\n   351→                    </div>\n   352→                </div>\n   353→\n   354→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   355→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/kepinski85/kempa-ai-devbox\" target=\"_blank\">Kempa AI Devbox</a></div>\n   356→                    <div class=\"product-description\">A self-hosted AI learning and building environment designed for Raspberry Pi, featuring multi-agent workflow for teaching programming and collaborating on projects.</div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   358→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   359→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   360→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-31</span>\n   361→                    </div>\n   362→                </div>\n   363→\n   364→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   365→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zabarich/danucode\" target=\"_blank\">Danucode</a></div>\n   366→                    <div class=\"product-description\">The simplest agent shell for your own models. Backend-agnostic terminal coding agent supporting Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.</div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   368→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   369→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   370→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-29</span>\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→\n   374→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   375→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/luminexo/trust\" target=\"_blank\">Trust</a></div>\n   376→                    <div class=\"product-description\">A shared terminal environment for pair programming with AI agents. Built with Rust, it provides a terminal-based IDE environment for collaborative AI-assisted programming.</div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   378→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   379→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   380→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-28</span>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                </div>\n   383→\n   384→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   385→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Swofty-Developments/CodeForge\" target=\"_blank\">CodeForge</a></div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"product-description\">An AI code editor that wraps Claude Code and Codex into a native desktop application with multi-thread sessions, an embedded browser, and a sleek dark UI.</div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   388→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   389→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   390→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-27</span>\n   391→                    </div>\n   392→                </div>\n   393→\n   394→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   395→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zdenham/anvil\" target=\"_blank\">Anvil</a></div>\n   396→                    <div class=\"product-description\">A desktop IDE designed specifically for parallel agent work. Enables isolated worktrees for parallel development without merge conflicts with first-class spec support.</div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   398→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   399→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   400→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-25</span>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                </div>\n   403→\n   404→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   405→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/JayCodesX/orager\" target=\"_blank\">Orager</a></div>\n   406→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Production-grade AI agent runtime and CLI built as the runtime behind Paperclip agents. Features multi-turn tool-calling, persistent memory, multimodal input, and multi-agent orchestration.</div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   408→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   409→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   410→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-24</span>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→\n   414→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   415→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/anYuJia/yode\" target=\"_blank\">Yode</a></div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Open-source AI coding agent for your terminal built in Rust. Reads, edits, searches, and runs commands from a single conversation with multi-provider support.</div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   418→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   419→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   420→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-23</span>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                </div>\n   423→\n   424→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   425→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zackbrooks84/continuum\" target=\"_blank\">continuum</a></div>\n   426→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Async task queue + persistent memory for AI agents that remembers everything, runs tasks while you sleep, and picks up exactly where you left off. Works with Claude Code Remote Control.</div>\n   427→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   428→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">code agent</span>\n   429→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   430→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-23</span>\n   431→                    </div>\n   432→                </div>\n   433→\n   434→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   435→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/AstrolexisAI/KCode\" target=\"_blank\">KCode</a></div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"product-description\">AI-powered coding assistant for the terminal that runs 100% local on your GPU. Features hardware-aware setup wizard, multi-GPU inference, 46 built-in tools, and local RAG engine.</div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   438→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   439→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   440→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-22</span>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                </div>\n   443→\n   444→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   445→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/tn3wman/forge\" target=\"_blank\">Forge</a></div>\n   446→                    <div class=\"product-description\">An agentic development environment that integrates Git client, GitHub dashboard, and AI agent workspace in one native desktop app. Runs multiple coding agents simultaneously.</div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   448→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   449→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   450→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-21</span>\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                </div>\n   453→\n   454→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   455→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nitkr/clean-sweep-cortex\" target=\"_blank\">Clean Sweep Cortex</a></div>\n   456→                    <div class=\"product-description\">A terminal-based AI coding agent specifically designed to help with cleaning WordPress malwares. Combines code analysis with security-focused workflows.</div>\n   457→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   458→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">workflow-specific tool</span>\n   459→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   460→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-29</span>\n   461→                    </div>\n   462→                </div>\n   463→\n   464→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   465→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nickleodoen/RewindAI\" target=\"_blank\">RewindAI</a></div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"product-description\">VS Code extension that gives AI coding agents version-controlled memory. Chat, commit, checkout — the agent remembers. Powered by Neo4j knowledge graph.</div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   468→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">code agent</span>\n   469→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   470→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-30</span>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                </div>\n   473→\n   474→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   475→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/AmanTShekar/zenith-terminal-buddy\" target=\"_blank\">Zenith Terminal Buddy</a></div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"product-description\">An interactive AI-powered pet mascot for VS Code that monitors terminal output to automatically catch and explain errors before you even have to ask. Makes AI assistance fun.</div>\n   477→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   478→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">IDE-integrated tool</span>\n   479→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   480→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-30</span>\n   481→                    </div>\n   482→                </div>\n   483→\n   484→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   485→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Rabba-Meghana/codebase-autocomplete-plugin\" target=\"_blank\">Codebase Autocomplete Plugin</a></div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Codebase-aware AI autocomplete plugin for JetBrains IDEs using RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), Groq, and ChromaDB. Provides intelligent code suggestions based on your entire codebase.</div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   488→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">IDE-integrated tool</span>\n   489→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   490→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-03-30</span>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                </div>\n   493→\n   494→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   495→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Peter08091996/waifu-code\" target=\"_blank\">Waifu Code</a></div>\n   496→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Open-source anime-style AI terminal coding assistant. Brings a unique aesthetic to terminal-based AI coding assistance.</div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   498→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   499→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   500→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-02</span>\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→\n   504→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   505→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/tienedev/claude-code-nix\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Nix</a></div>\n   506→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Nix flake for Claude Code providing AI coding assistant in your terminal with auto-updated daily builds and reproducible Nix-based installation.</div>\n   507→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   508→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   509→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-01</span>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                </div>\n   513→\n   514→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   515→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/pookieclaw/camel-code\" target=\"_blank\">Camel Code</a></div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Terminal AI coding assistant written in OCaml combining functional programming robustness with modern AI capabilities for a unique 'two humps, zero runtime' approach.</div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   518→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   520→                        <span class=\"tag\">2026-04-01</span>\n   521→                    </div>\n   522→                </div>\n   523→\n   524→                <div class=\"product-item\">\n   525→                    <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/0x94t3z/mini-codex\" target=\"_blank\">Mini Codex</a></div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"product-description\">Terminal coding assistant with workspace-scoped file tools and multi-provider support (Gemini, OpenAI, OpenRouter, xAI). Lightweight alternative for AI-assisted coding.</div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n   528→                        <span class=\"tag category-tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   529→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   530→                        